    "content": "# Surah Aal 'Imran (آل عمران) — Part 4 of 6: Verses 92–120\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah Aal 'Imran (The Family of Imran)**, covering **Verses 92–120**. This lesson is part of the comprehensive FAHMRISE Qur'an Tafsir curriculum, designed to cultivate deep understanding (Fahm), spiritual elevation (Rise), and principled action.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 3 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة آل عمران |\n| **English Meaning** | The Family of Imran |\n| **Lesson Part** | Part 4 of 6 |\n| **Verses Covered** | Verses 92–120 (29 verses) |\n| **Classification** | Madani Revelation |\n| **Thematic Focus** | The Rope of Allah, The Best Community & True Righteousness |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Context & Circumstances of Revelation (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nVerse 103 was revealed when a Jewish instigator named Shas ibn Qays saw the Aws and Khazraj tribes sitting together in peaceful brotherhood in Madinah and hired a youth to recite pre-Islamic war poetry (Battle of Bu'ath) to provoke them into drawing swords against each other, until the Prophet ﷺ rushed to them, rebuking: 'Do you call to the calls of Jahiliyyah while I am among you?!'\n\nScholars of Tafsir (including Imam al-Wahidi and Imam as-Suyuti) highlight that grasping the historical backdrop and authentic occasions of revelation provides an essential anchor for correctly interpreting divine intent and extracting universal legal and spiritual principles.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 92–97: Sacrificial Charity and the Sanctuary of Bakkah\n\nYou will not attain piety until you spend from what you love (inspiring Abu Talhah to give away his beloved Bairuha' garden). The first house of worship appointed for mankind was that at Bakkah—blessed and a guidance for the worlds, containing clear signs such as the Station of Ibrahim (Maqam Ibrahim); pilgrimage is a duty for all who can find a way.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 98–109: The Rope of Allah and Overcoming Tribal Polarization\n\nO you who believe, fear Allah as He deserves to be feared, and do not die except as Muslims. Hold fast to the rope of Allah together and do not become divided. Remember Allah's favor when you were enemies and He united your hearts so that you became brothers. Let there arise from you a group inviting to all good, enjoining righteousness and forbidding wrong.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 110–120: The Best Nation and Warning Against Treacherous Intimates\n\nYou are the best community produced for mankind: you enjoin good, forbid evil, and believe in Allah. Some of the People of Scripture are devout believers reciting verses throughout the night. Do not take as intimate advisors those outside your faith who do not spare any effort to corrupt you, wishing for your distress; their hatred has shown from their mouths, and what their breasts conceal is greater.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances (Gharib al-Qur'an)\n\n- **Lan Tanalu al-Birra (لَن تَنَالُوا۟ ٱلْبِرَّ)**: 'Never will you attain true righteousness until you spend from that which you love dearly.'\n- **Bakkah (بَكَّةَ)**: The ancient, blessed name of Makkah—the first sanctuary of worship established for mankind.\n- **Wa'tasimu bi-Habli-Llahi (وَٱعْتَصِمُوا۟ بِحَبْلِ ٱللَّهِ)**: And hold fast, all together, to the unbreakable rope of Allah (His Qur'an and Deen), and do not divide.\n- **Khayra Ummah (خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ)**: The best community brought forth for humanity—conditioned upon enjoining righteousness, preventing evil, and believing in Allah.\n- **Bitana (بِطَانَةً)**: An intimate inner circle, confidants who gain access to your secret strategies and vulnerabilities.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Tier Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah Aal 'Imran transform daily character, classical scholars emphasize contextualizing its guidance across life stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** When you donate toys or clothes to poor children, give nice, clean ones that you would love to play with, not broken rubbish.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Be very careful who you let into your close circle of friends (Bitanah); real friends encourage you to do good and protect your secrets.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Prioritize community unity: do not allow political polarization, tribalism, or ethnic chauvinism to shatter the sacred brotherhood of Islam.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Select an item of personal wealth you deeply cherish (favorite garment, savings, precious time) and donate it to a noble cause to fulfill verse 92.**\n2. **Actively reconcile between two estranged Muslim brothers or family members to fulfill 'Wa'tasimu bi-Habli-Llah'.**\n3. **Fulfill your responsibility as part of the 'Khayra Ummah' by gently encouraging righteousness and speaking out against injustice.**\n",
