    "content": "# Surah An-Nisa (النساء) — Part 3 of 6: Verses 43–70\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah An-Nisa (The Women)**, covering **Verses 43–70**. This lesson is part of the comprehensive FAHMRISE Qur'an Tafsir curriculum, designed to cultivate deep understanding (Fahm), spiritual elevation (Rise), and principled action.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 4 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة النساء |\n| **English Meaning** | The Women |\n| **Lesson Part** | Part 3 of 6 |\n| **Verses Covered** | Verses 43–70 (28 verses) |\n| **Classification** | Madani Revelation |\n| **Thematic Focus** | Purity in Worship, Judicial Justice & Constitutional Governance |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Context & Circumstances of Revelation (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nVerse 58 was revealed on the day of the Conquest of Makkah when the Prophet ﷺ took the key to the Ka'bah from Uthman ibn Talhah, and Allah revealed the command to return trusts to their owners, so the Prophet ﷺ returned the key to Uthman and his family permanently.\n\nScholars of Tafsir (including Imam al-Wahidi and Imam as-Suyuti) highlight that grasping the historical backdrop and authentic occasions of revelation provides an essential anchor for correctly interpreting divine intent and extracting universal legal and spiritual principles.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 43–57: Purity for Prayer, Shirk the Unpardonable Sin, and Hellfire\n\nDo not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you are saying, nor in major impurity without bathing, unless passing through. If sick or traveling without water, perform Tayammum with clean soil. Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. Those who disbelieve will have their skins replaced in Fire to taste continuous retribution; believers dwell in cool, perpetual shade.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 58–63: The Constitutional Core: Fulfilling Trusts and Absolute Justice\n\n'Indeed, Allah commands you to render trusts to whom they are due, and when you judge between people to judge with justice.' O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. If you disagree over anything, refer it back to Allah and the Messenger if you truly believe in Allah and the Last Day. Exposing hypocrites who seek arbitration from Taghut while claiming to want only goodwill.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 64–70: Submitting to Prophetic Judgment and the Lofty Companionship\n\nBy your Lord, they will not truly believe until they make you, [O Muhammad], judge concerning that over which they dispute among themselves, and find no distress in their souls and submit in full submission. Whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger—those will be with the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor: of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth (Siddiqin), the martyrs (Shuhada'), and the righteous (Salihin). What excellent companions!\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances (Gharib al-Qur'an)\n\n- **Tayammum (تَيَمَّمُوا۟)**: Dry ablution using clean, wholesome earth/dust when water is absent or medically harmful.\n- **Ash-Shirk (ٱلشِّرْكَ)**: Associating partners with Allah—the supreme unpardonable injustice if one dies unrepentant.\n- **Al-Amanat (ٱلْأَمَٰنَٰتِ)**: Trusts—all moral, financial, legal, and public duties entrusted to human responsibility.\n- **Uli al-Amri minkum (أُو۟لِى ٱلْأَمْرِ مِنكُم)**: Those in legitimate authority among you—just rulers, judges, and qualified scholars.\n- **Ar-Rafiqu al-A'la (ٱلرَّفِيقِ ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ)**: The highest, noblest companionship in Paradise: prophets, truthful affirmers, martyrs, and the righteous.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Tier Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah An-Nisa transform daily character, classical scholars emphasize contextualizing its guidance across life stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Always return borrowed things (toys, books, pencils) to their owners in perfect shape; returning trusts is an order from Allah.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** When friends have an argument, don't take sides based on who is cooler; stand up for the one who is telling the truth with fairness.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Recognize verse 59 as the cornerstone of Islamic constitutional law: every leader's policy must be bounded by the Qur'an and authentic Sunnah.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Return any entrusted items, unpaid debts, or borrowed equipment to their rightful owners immediately (4:58).**\n2. **Learn and practice the simple method of Tayammum (striking clean dust and wiping face and hands) for medical or travel emergencies.**\n3. **Supplicate to be joined with the four blessed categories of verse 69: 'Allahumma ij'alna ma'a an-nabiyyina was-siddiqina wash-shuhada'i was-salihin'.**\n",
    "practicalApplication": "Incorporate Surah An-Nisa (Verses 43–70) into your daily reflection and voluntary prayers. Focus upon its central theme: Purity in Worship, Judicial Justice & Constitutional Governance. Commit to implementing its practical action steps in your home, studies, and workplace.",
