    "content": "# Surah At-Tawbah (التوبة) — Part 1 of 5: Verses 1–28\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah At-Tawbah (The Repentance)**, covering **Verses 1–28**. This lesson is part of the comprehensive FAHMRISE Qur'an Tafsir curriculum, designed to cultivate deep understanding (Fahm), spiritual elevation (Rise), and principled action.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 9 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة التوبة |\n| **English Meaning** | The Repentance |\n| **Lesson Part** | Part 1 of 5 |\n| **Verses Covered** | Verses 1–28 (28 verses) |\n| **Classification** | Madani Revelation |\n| **Thematic Focus** | Bara'ah: Renunciation of Treaties, Asylum for Seekers & Custodians of the Sacred Sanctuary |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Context & Circumstances of Revelation (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed in late 9 AH following the Conquest of Makkah and prior to the Farewell Pilgrimage, when the Prophet ﷺ dispatched 'Ali ibn Abi Talib to proclaim these verses at the pilgrimage season (Yawm al-Hajj al-Akbar), announcing that no polytheist may perform Hajj after this year and no unclad person may circumambulate the Ka'bah.\n\nScholars of Tafsir (including Imam al-Wahidi and Imam as-Suyuti) highlight that grasping the historical backdrop and authentic occasions of revelation provides an essential anchor for correctly interpreting divine intent and extracting universal legal and spiritual principles.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 1–6: The Proclamation of Bara'ah and the Sacred Asylum Mandate\n\nFreedom from obligation from Allah and His Messenger to those polytheists with whom you made treaties. Travel freely throughout the land for four months, but know that you cannot evade Allah. An announcement from Allah and His Messenger on the day of the Greater Pilgrimage that Allah is disassociated from the idolaters, as is His Messenger. If they repent and establish prayer and give zakah, they are your brethren in religion. If any idolater seeks your asylum, grant him asylum so that he may hear the words of Allah, and then deliver him to his place of safety, because they are a people who do not know.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 7–16: Treachery of Treaty-Breakers and Testing Sincerity\n\nHow can there be a treaty with polytheists except those with whom you made a covenant at the Sacred Mosque? As long as they are true to you, be true to them. How can it be when, if they gain dominance over you, they do not respect kinship or covenant? They satisfy you with their mouths while their hearts refuse, and most of them are defiantly disobedient. They traded the signs of Allah for a cheap price and averted people from His path. Fight them; Allah will punish them by your hands, disgrace them, heal the breasts of a believing people, and remove the fury from their hearts. Do you think you will be left without Allah testing which of you strive and take no intimate confidant besides Allah, His Messenger, and the believers?\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 17–28: True Custodians of Mosques and Sanctity of the Ka'bah\n\nIt is not for polytheists to maintain the mosques of Allah while witnessing against themselves with disbelief. Only those shall visit and maintain the mosques of Allah who believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish prayer, give zakah, and fear none except Allah. Do you consider providing water to pilgrims and tending the Sacred Mosque equal to one who believes in Allah and the Last Day and strives in His cause? They are not equal in Allah's sight. Those who believed and emigrated and strove with their wealth and lives have the greatest rank with Allah. O believers, the polytheists are spiritually impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque after this year. If you fear poverty, Allah will enrich you from His bounty if He wills.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances (Gharib al-Qur'an)\n\n- **Bara'ah (بَرَآءَةٌ)**: A complete declaration of dissociation, acquittal, and immunity from covenants.\n- **Fasihu (فَسِيحُوا۟)**: 'Travel freely, securely, and unmolested' during the designated four sacred months of grace.\n- **Fa-ajirhu (فَأَجِرْهُ)**: 'Grant him asylum and safe protection' so that he may hear the divine speech of Allah.\n- **La yarqubuna illan wa-la dhimmah (لَا يَرْقُبُونَ إِلًّا وَلَا ذِمَّةً)**: 'They respect neither kinship ties (ill) nor covenants of honor (dhimmah)' regarding a believer.\n- **Ya'muru masajid Allah (يَعْمُرُ مَسَـٰجِدَ ٱللَّهِ)**: 'Maintains and populates the mosques of Allah' through sincere worship, physical upkeep, and righteous deeds.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Tier Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah At-Tawbah transform daily character, classical scholars emphasize contextualizing its guidance across life stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Mosques are houses of Allah: keep them clean, speak politely inside, and welcome everyone who comes to pray.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Notice verse 9:6: Islam commands Muslims to protect even an ideological opponent seeking knowledge and ensure their safe journey home.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Recognize that external status or heritage (like serving water to pilgrims) means nothing without internal faith, prayer, charity, and striving in truth.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Attend the congregational prayer at your local mosque and contribute toward its physical maintenance and community programs.**\n2. **Read verse 9:6 carefully to articulate Islam's ethical rules regarding asylum, refuge, and respectful intellectual dialogue.**\n3. **Check your personal relationships to ensure that agreements, promises, and contracts are fulfilled with total trustworthiness.**\n",
    "practicalApplication": "Incorporate Surah At-Tawbah (Verses 1–28) into your daily reflection and voluntary prayers. Focus upon its central theme: Bara'ah: Renunciation of Treaties, Asylum for Seekers & Custodians of the Sacred Sanctuary. Commit to implementing its practical action steps in your home, studies, and workplace.",
