    "content": "# Surah At-Tawbah (التوبة) — Part 3 of 5: Verses 43–72\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah At-Tawbah (The Repentance)**, covering **Verses 43–72**. This lesson is part of the comprehensive FAHMRISE Qur'an Tafsir curriculum, designed to cultivate deep understanding (Fahm), spiritual elevation (Rise), and principled action.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 9 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة التوبة |\n| **English Meaning** | The Repentance |\n| **Lesson Part** | Part 3 of 5 |\n| **Verses Covered** | Verses 43–72 (30 verses) |\n| **Classification** | Madani Revelation |\n| **Thematic Focus** | The Expedition of Tabuk: Unmasking Hypocrisy vs. The Alliance of True Believers |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Context & Circumstances of Revelation (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed regarding the strenuous Expedition to Tabuk ('Ghazwat al-'Usrah' / the Campaign of Hardship) during intense summer heat and crop ripening, when hypocrites made up flimsy excuses to stay behind, and mocked Abu 'Aqil who worked all night lifting dates to donate a single measure of dates.\n\nScholars of Tafsir (including Imam al-Wahidi and Imam as-Suyuti) highlight that grasping the historical backdrop and authentic occasions of revelation provides an essential anchor for correctly interpreting divine intent and extracting universal legal and spiritual principles.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 43–59: Testing Times at Tabuk and the Evasion of Hypocrites\n\nMay Allah pardon you! Why did you give them permission to remain behind until it was clear to you who was truthful and you knew who was lying? Those who believe in Allah and the Last Day would not ask you for exemption from striving with their wealth and lives. Only those ask your permission who do not believe in Allah and the Last Day and whose hearts are in doubt. If they had intended to go forth, they would have made preparations, but Allah disliked their going forth so He kept them back. If they had gone out with you, they would only have increased you in disorder and hurried about spreading slander. Say: 'Nothing will ever happen to us except what Allah has decreed for us; He is our Protector, and upon Allah let the believers rely.' They swear by Allah that they are from among you, but they are not; rather they are a people terrified. Among them are those who criticize you concerning charity: if given from it they are pleased, but if not given, they are enraged.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 60–66: Mockery of Faith and the Reality of Divine Boundaries\n\nAmong them are those who hurt the Prophet and say 'He is an ear (believes everything)'. Say: 'An ear of good for you; he believes in Allah and believes the faithful believers and is a mercy to those who believe among you.' Do they not know that whoever opposes Allah and His Messenger—for him is the fire of Hell wherein he will abide eternally? The hypocrites fear lest a Surah be revealed exposing what is in their hearts. Say: 'Mock on! Indeed Allah will bring forth that which you fear.' If you ask them, they will surely say: 'We were only conversing and playing.' Say: 'Is it Allah and His verses and His Messenger that you were mocking? Make no excuse; you have disbelieved after your belief.'\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 67–72: The Anatomy of Hypocrites vs. The Fellowship of Believers\n\nThe hypocrite men and hypocrite women are of one another: they enjoin what is wrong and forbid what is right and close their hands tightly. They have forgotten Allah, so He has forgotten them. Indeed, the hypocrites are the defiantly disobedient. Allah has promised the hypocrite men, women, and disbelievers the fire of Hell. But the believing men and believing women are allies of one another: they enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, establish prayer, give zakah, and obey Allah and His Messenger. Those—Allah will have mercy upon them. Indeed, Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise. Allah has promised the believing men and women gardens beneath which rivers flow, and beautiful dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence; but the greatest bliss is the good pleasure of Allah (wa-ridwanun mina Allahi akbar); that is the supreme success.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Scholarly Exegesis (Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di, Akhsaru Tafaseer):** Classical commentators emphasize that these verses establish divine guidance, moral accountability, and spiritual elevation, providing clear criteria for personal ethics and communal governance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances (Gharib al-Qur'an)\n\n- **'Afa Allahu 'anka (عَفَا ٱللَّهُ عَنكَ)**: 'May Allah pardon you!'—an opening of extraordinary divine gentleness and honor before inquiring.\n- **Fi al-harri (فِى ٱلْحَرِّ)**: 'In the blistering heat'—the hypocrites' excuse to evade the long march to Tabuk.\n- **Yalmizuna (يَلْمِزُونَ)**: 'They sneer at, ridicule, and defame' the charitable believers.\n- **Yaqbiduna aydiyahum (يَقْبِضُونَ أَيْدِيَهُمْ)**: 'They clench their hands tightly'—stingy, withholding charity and righteous spending.\n- **Awliya'u ba'd (أَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍ)**: 'Allies, protectors, and supporting helpers of one another'—the mutual bond of believing men and women.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Multi-Tier Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah At-Tawbah transform daily character, classical scholars emphasize contextualizing its guidance across life stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Never make fun of someone's honest gift: whether it is a single coin or a big prize, Allah loves sincerity most.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Be very mindful of what you joke about: joking about religion or making fun of sacred verses is a grave moral error (9:65).\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Compare verses 9:67 and 9:71: hypocrites drag each other down into cynicism, whereas believers uplift each other into worship, charity, and public good.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Memorize verse 9:51: 'Qul lan yusibana illa ma kataba Allahu lana...' as a spiritual shield against anxiety and fear.**\n2. **Support and encourage your fellow community members in goodness without ever belittling anyone's small charitable contribution.**\n3. **Check your social circle: ensure your closest friends are people who encourage prayer, truthfulness, and generous giving.**\n",
